Patch 41. In the series since 2026-10-17, after patch 40.

BitStream (src/core/bit_stream.cpp) is big-endian: Peek, and Read through it, swap the 8 bytes
they load. Write did not, so it masked and stored the value in the opposite byte order, and its
end-of-stream assert was off by one (>= where Peek has >). Four stream_test cases were disabled
with SKIP("BitStream::Write is broken - doesn't byte-swap on store") and [!mayfail]. Write now
swaps on load and on store, as Peek does, and asserts as Peek does. Nothing in the runtime calls
BitStream::Write (the XMA decoder only reads), so no behaviour changes; the cases run again.

Test: the four cases without SKIP, and the 16-bit one also checks the bytes in memory (0x12,
0x34). Without the change 6 assertions fail; with it all [bitstream] cases pass on Linux. With
patches 39-41 no SDK test is skipped (Linux ctest: 1768 of 1768, none skipped).

diff --git a/src/core/bit_stream.cpp b/src/core/bit_stream.cpp
index 9329c6d..e452c55 100644
--- a/src/core/bit_stream.cpp
+++ b/src/core/bit_stream.cpp
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@ uint64_t BitStream::Read(size_t num_bits) {
 // TODO: This is totally not tested!
 bool BitStream::Write(uint64_t val, size_t num_bits) {
   assert_false(num_bits > 57);
-  assert_false(offset_bits_ + num_bits >= size_bits_);
+  assert_false(offset_bits_ + num_bits > size_bits_);
 
   size_t offset_bytes = offset_bits_ >> 3;
   size_t rel_offset_bits = offset_bits_ - (offset_bytes << 3);
@@ -86,7 +86,8 @@ bool BitStream::Write(uint64_t val, size_t num_bits) {
 
   // offset ----->
   // ....[junk]...| target bits w/ junk |....[junk]......
-  uint64_t bits = *(uint64_t*)(buffer_ + offset_bytes);
+  // The stream is big-endian, as Peek reads it: swap into the same order before masking.
+  uint64_t bits = rex::byte_swap(*(uint64_t*)(buffer_ + offset_bytes));
 
   // AND with mask
   // ....[junk]...| target bits (0) |........[junk]......
@@ -96,8 +97,8 @@ bool BitStream::Write(uint64_t val, size_t num_bits) {
   // ....[junk]...| target bits (val) |......[junk]......
   bits |= val;
 
-  // Store into the bitstream.
-  *(uint64_t*)(buffer_ + offset_bytes) = bits;
+  // Store into the bitstream, back in its byte order.
+  *(uint64_t*)(buffer_ + offset_bytes) = rex::byte_swap(bits);
 
   // Advance the bitstream forward.
   Advance(num_bits);
